            "display_name": "Gemini",
            "execution_status": "SUCCESS",
            "provider": "gemini",
            "rank": 1,
            "reason": "Constellation is a primary beneficiary of the 'nuclear renaissance' as tech hyperscalers secure carbon-free baseload power. Recent regulatory wins, including a FERC waiver for capacity rights transfer to the Crane Clean Energy Center (Three Mile Island), accelerate its 2027 restart timeline. Higher full-year EPS guidance ($12.50) and nuclear's scarcity value provide a resilient long-term fundamental floor with technical bullishness.",
            "risk": "Regulatory or interconnection delays with the PJM grid, which could push the Crane Center's revenue generation beyond current 2027 estimates.",
            "score": 90,
            "selected": true
          },
          {
            "display_name": "DeepSeek",
            "execution_status": "SUCCESS",
            "provider": "deepseek",
            "rank": 1,
            "reason": "Constellation just raised FY26 adjusted EPS guidance to $11.50–$12.50, a midpoint roughly 28% above last year, and holds long-duration PPAs with Microsoft (Crane restart, ~$16B) and Meta (Clinton), plus the $715M RISEC acquisition. The nuclear/AI power demand story gives visible growth, and at least one estimate pegs shares ~24% below fair value, with utility defensiveness suited to the current tape.",
            "risk": "Despite positive news, CEG fell 2.7% on Sep 10, suggesting much AI-power enthusiasm is already priced in; a further rise in Treasury yields would pressure utility valuations near term.",
            "score": 60,
            "selected": true
          },
